    "lawCode": "Amd §1402, N-PC L",
    "lawSection": "Not-for-Profit Corporation Law",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S8179\n\nTITLE OF BILL:\nAn act to amend the not-for-profit corporation law, in relation to an\nexemption to the residency requirement for firefighters of the Huguenot\nFire Co., Inc.\n\nPURPOSE:\nTo include the Huguenot Fire Co., Inc. in Orange County among the list\nof fire districts and fire companies which are exempt from the statutory\nlimits on the percentage of non-resident members, thereby helping enable\nthis volunteer fire company to have a sufficient level of membership to\nprotect the community.\n\nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\nSection 1. Amends Subparagraph 3 of paragraph (c) of section 1402 of the\nnot-for-profit corporation law, as amended by chapter 351 of the laws of\n2000 to exempt the Huguenot Fire Company, Inc. located in the town of\nDeerpark in Orange County from the requirement that the percentage of\nnon-resident members of a fire department cannot exceed 45% of the total\nmembership of the department.\n\nSection 2. Effective Date\n\nEXISTING LAW:\nSection 1402 of the not-for-profit corporation law generally provides\nthat the percentage of non-resident members of a fire department cannot\nexceed 45% of the total membership of the department.  However, a\nsignificant number of Fire Companies and Districts have been exempted\nfrom this requirement in recent years.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\nThis legislation is critically important for the Huguenot Fire Co.,\nInc.'s ability to recruit and retain volunteer members.\n\nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\nNew Bill.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\nNone.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately.\n\n",
